        "type": "question",
        "question": {
          "id": 337545,
          "format": "MC",
          "difficulty": 2,
          "exampleId": 6618,
          "text": "<p>Consider the following differential equation\n\\[\ny'' - 2y' + y = \\dfrac{e^{x}}{x}.\n\\]</p>\n<p>The general solution to this equation can be written as\n\\[\ny(x) = A e^x + B x e^x + g(x),\n\\]\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are constants. Which of the following could be the function $g(x)?$</p>\n<p><em>Hint: Use the variation of parameters method.</em></p>\n",
          "choice1": " $x^2e^x\\ln|x|$",
          "choice2": " $4xe^{x}\\ln|x|$",
          "choice3": " $xe^x\\ln|x|$",
          "choice4": " $2x^2e^x\\ln|x|$",
          "choice5": " $2xe^x\\ln|x|$",
