          "format": "MC",
          "difficulty": 2,
          "exampleId": 6617,
          "text": "<p>Consider the following differential equation\n\\[\ny''-2y'+2y=e^x \\sec x.\n\\]</p>\n<p>The general solution to this equation can be written as\n\\[\ny(x)=R e^x\\cos x+Q e^x\\sin x+g(x),\n\\]\nwhere $R$ and $Q$ are constants. Which of the following could be the function $g(x)?$</p>\n<p><em>Hint: Use the variation of parameters method.</em></p>\n",
          "choice1": " $e^x\\sin{x} + xe^x\\cos{x}$",
          "choice2": " $e^x\\cos x\\ln|\\sin x|+xe^x\\sin x$",
          "choice3": " $e^x\\sin x\\ln|\\cos x|+xe^x\\cos x$",
          "choice4": " $e^x\\cos x+xe^x\\sin x$",
          "choice5": " $e^x\\cos x\\ln|\\cos x|+xe^x\\sin x$\n",
          "freeAnswerChoice": " ",
          "number": 3,
